53
00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.880
First of all, maybe a term you haven't heard before.

54
00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.760
If you think about skills

55
00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:52.840
and authoring them, the barrier to entry is super low, right?

56
00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.480
They're mostly just text files.

57
00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.800
Sometimes you might put a couple of scripts in there with them.

58
00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.960
It's super easy to add your own new ones or install third party ones from GitHub.

59
00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.160
They're also pretty powerful as well, right?

60
00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.760
Like, it's very easy to write a small amount of text and influence

61
00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.840
how the agents works in quite a powerful way.

62
00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.920
And so because of this, teams are facing this kind of

63
00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.240
Cambrian explosion of skills within their organizations.

64
00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.160
Guy mentioned in his slides this morning, we have 2 million

65
00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.160
plus skills across GitHub, across 44,000 repos.

66
00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.320
That's an insane amount.

67
00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.120
That's obviously just the public ones as well.

68
00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.880
I'm sure it's even higher in terms of internal private repos

69
00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.840
and private skills as well.

70
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.840
So yeah, we're seeing skills spread across lots of different locations.

71
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.560
So and GitHub, as I mentioned, across things like Claude Marketplaces

72
00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.600
and also on developers, local machines as well.

73
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:45.960
Right.

74
00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.360
It's hard to get visibility around where skills are being used.

75
00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:50.560
And if you can't track that,

76
00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:53.480
then you can't measure that and you can't improve things. Right?

77
00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.840
So this is a real problem right now that we're hearing from customers.

